- **The Kitchen Nesting Analogy**:
  • **JVM**: The stove that cooks the meal (executes the bytecode).
  • **JRE**: The entire kitchen containing the stove plus pantry ingredients and spices (JVM + standard library classes).
  • **JDK**: The whole culinary institute with the kitchen, plus chef knives, recipe manuals, and training tools (JRE + javac, javadoc, debugger).', '- "JDK is the development kit containing the compiler (javac), debugger, and development tools plus the JRE."
