  5. Boolean Literals (`true`, `false`)
  6. Null Literal (`null`)',
  simple_meaning = '- If a variable is a label on a cardboard box, the literal is the actual physical item you place inside that box. In `int age = 25;`, `age` is the variable identifier and `25` is the numeric literal.',
