class Parent {
    public static void identify() {
        System.out.println("Static method inside Parent");
    }
    public void describe() {
        System.out.println("Instance method inside Parent");
    }
}

class Child extends Parent {
    // Hiding: declares same static method
    public static void identify() {
        System.out.println("Static method inside Child");
    }
    // Overriding: overrides instance method
    @Override
    public void describe() {
        System.out.println("Instance method inside Child");
    }
}

public class MethodHidingDemo {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Parent ref = new Child();

        // 1. Static call: Early bound to Parent reference type!
        ref.identify(); // Outputs: Static method inside Parent

        // 2. Instance call: Dynamic dispatch to Child object!
        ref.describe(); // Outputs: Instance method inside Child

        // Proper invocation of static methods should use class names:
        Parent.identify(); // Parent
        Child.identify();  // Child
    }
}

### Output & Execution Mechanics
- `ref.identify()` outputs `Parent` because static methods bind to the reference type `Parent` during compilation.
- `ref.describe()` outputs `Child` because instance methods bind to the runtime object `Child` via dynamic dispatch.', 'In production Java systems, Method Hiding & Static Method Binding is used to guarantee reliability and performance. Key architectural considerations include proper design patterns, memory awareness, and adhering to language specifications.', 'Refer to standard code example demonstrating proper syntax and execution.', 'Method call resolved by reference type at compile-time.'),
(101, 1, 'Advanced', 3, 1, 1, 'What tricky edge cases, common pitfalls, or interview traps are associated with Method Hiding & Static Method Binding?', 'Be cautious with null handling, type compatibility, and concurrency rules with Method Hiding & Static Method Binding.', '| Dimension | Method Overriding (Instance Methods) | Method Hiding (Static Methods) |
|---|---|---|
| **Modifier** | Non-static | `static` |
| **Binding Time** | Runtime (Late / Dynamic Binding) | Compile-time (Early / Static Binding) |
| **Resolution Criteria** | Actual Object in Heap | Reference Variable Type |
| **Polymorphism** | Achieves runtime polymorphism | No polymorphism; compile-time selection |
| **@Override Allowed?** | Yes, highly recommended | No; compiler will throw an error |

### Comparison Reference
| Dimension | Method Overriding (Instance Methods) | Method Hiding (Static Methods) |
|---|---|---|
| **Modifier** | Non-static | `static` |
| **Binding Time** | Runtime (Late / Dynamic Binding) | Compile-time (Early / Static Binding) |
| **Resolution Criteria** | Actual Object in Heap | Reference Variable Type |
| **Polymorphism** | Achieves runtime polymorphism | No polymorphism; compile-time selection |
| **@Override Allowed?** | Yes, highly recommended | No; compiler will throw an error |', 'In interviews, highlight the non-obvious nuances: - "Method hiding happens when a subclass defines a static method with the exact signature of a superclass static method."
- "Because static methods belong to the class, the compiler binds the call based on the reference type, not the runtime object. Hence, static methods cannot be overridden."', 'Production edge-case scenarios and code maintenance.', 'Always invoke static methods using the ClassName directly.');

