- **Owning a Delivery Truck vs Hiring a Courier Service**:
  • Extending `Thread` is like manufacturing your own custom delivery truck just to deliver a parcel. You are locked in and cannot extend any other vehicle.
  • Implementing `Runnable` is writing the shipping label (the task) and handing it to an existing courier service (`Thread` or `ExecutorService`). Your class is still free to inherit from any other business class.', '- "Implementing Runnable is preferred over extending Thread because Java allows single class inheritance, and Runnable cleanly separates the task logic from thread execution."
- "Runnable also integrates seamlessly with ExecutorService thread pools and Lambda expressions."', '- **Owning a Delivery Truck vs Hiring a Courier Service**:
